@lang en
IMPORT prelude

-- Figures this row takes from the National Insurance Institute's own publications, because the
-- Law states the rule that produces them but not the figure. Each carries the URL, the retrieval
-- time and the sha256 of the bytes fetched. The pages were fetched with curl on 2026-10-06 and are
-- not deposited (the site reserves its rights); NOTES.md section 7 transcribes what each says.
-- The site describes its content as general information and not the binding text of the Law, so
-- each figure here is an official publication of a computed amount, not law: the rules that make
-- it are in nii-s1-definitions.l4 and nii-s334-interpretation.l4.
--
-- Only figures the rules may use are here. Figures used only as test expectations (the composite
-- rates and the worked example the Institute prints) are in the tests modules, with the same
-- provenance.

§ `Figures published by the National Insurance Institute`

§§ `The reduced collection threshold for 2026`

-- s 334(a) "reduced collection threshold": 7,522 NIS, updated on 1 January 2026 by the rise in
-- the consumer price index (s 334(a)(1)). The Institute's rates pages print the result:
--   "on monthly income up to 7,703 NIS (reduced rate)" ... "(from 01.01.2026)"
-- on each of three pages, fetched 2026-10-06:
--   https://www.btl.gov.il/Insurance/Rates/Pages/%d7%9c%d7%a2%d7%95%d7%91%d7%93%d7%99%d7%9d%20%d7%a9%d7%9b%d7%99%d7%a8%d7%99%d7%9d.aspx
--     (employees) 14:07:32Z, sha256 63457694f21874d7e1eee490811ec86b60c83aff49f733aae6aadb85b9129aba
--   https://www.btl.gov.il/Insurance/Rates/Pages/%d7%9c%d7%a2%d7%a6%d7%9e%d7%90%d7%99%d7%9d.aspx
--     (self-employed) 14:07:34Z, sha256 5abe5977d369d0da10e26269ab90aec5ae216247b6018e6721ba760fc7d33f22
--   https://www.btl.gov.il/Insurance/Rates/Pages/%d7%9e%d7%99%20%d7%a9%d7%90%d7%99%d7%a0%d7%9d%20%d7%a2%d7%95%d7%91%d7%93%d7%99%d7%9d%20%d7%95%d7%91%d7%a2%d7%9c%d7%99%20%d7%94%d7%9b%d7%a0%d7%a1%d7%94%20%d7%a9%d7%9c%d7%90%20%d7%9e%d7%a2%d7%91%d7%95%d7%93%d7%94.aspx
--     (neither) 14:07:36Z, sha256 36c88a5e9666a9410a13dbe50ebdb0778b2653305d0a33688682029edd24d183
-- The consolidation's editorial note on s 334 gives the same figure (an aid, not authority):
-- src:3605 | ”מדרגת גבייה מופחתת“ – סכום של 7,522 שקלים חדשים [note: (נקוב לשנת 2025; בשנת 2026, 7,703 ש״ח)], כשהוא מעודכן ב־1 בינואר של כל שנה כלהלן:
@ref National Insurance Institute, rates pages for employees, the self-employed and those who are neither, fetched 2026-10-06 (sha256 above); s 334(a) (source line 3605)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the reduced collection threshold for 2026, as published by the National Insurance Institute` MEANS 7_703

§§ `The average wage from 1 January 2026`

-- s 1 "the average wage" is updated on 1 January of each tax year (and when compensation applies).
-- The Institute publishes it twice, "under section 1" and "under section 2" (s 2 changes the
-- calculation for exceptional pay months, "for benefits and contributions"), each "for benefits"
-- and "for contributions". From 01.01.2026 all four are published, and the two "for contributions"
-- figures are 13,566 (section 1) and 13,769 (section 2). Fetched 2026-10-06 14:08:43Z:
--   https://www.btl.gov.il/Mediniyut/GeneralData/Pages/%d7%a9%d7%9b%d7%a8%20%d7%9e%d7%9e%d7%95%d7%a6%d7%a2.aspx
--   sha256 fe4d43b1bc1f007839567cbee759f8135558c94c89e3a10a531b5baecaf31b1f
-- The consolidation's editorial notes give the same two figures (aids, not authority):
-- src:226 | [note: השכר הממוצע לפי הגדרה זאת: בשנת 2026, 13,566 ש״ח.]
-- src:233 | [note: נכון לשנת 2026, השכר הממוצע המדוד הוא 13,769 ש״ח.]
-- Which of the two a provision in this row means by "the average wage" is fork F5 in NOTES.md;
-- the rules take the average wage as an argument, and the tests say which figure they supply.
@ref National Insurance Institute, "average wage under sections 1 and 2", fetched 2026-10-06 (sha256 above); s 1 "השכר הממוצע" (source lines 222-226)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the average wage from 1 January 2026 under section 1, for contributions, as published by the National Insurance Institute` MEANS 13_566

@ref National Insurance Institute, "average wage under sections 1 and 2", fetched 2026-10-06 (sha256 above); s 2(b) (source lines 236-238)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the average wage from 1 January 2026 as calculated under section 2, for contributions, as published by the National Insurance Institute` MEANS 13_769
